# CH11 — Below the Coronation. Sable Conduit: relays, lifts, Soldiers' Walk, Marshal Bridge (B09).

@scene D09_ENTER once
music M020
say narr | The old aqueduct under Veyr. The water is gone; cable runs where it used to flow. Somewhere above, bells are ringing for a coronation nobody announced.
say nera | Eight of us, one tunnel. We can't all fight in a corridor this narrow.
say oriel | Four in front, four behind carrying the lamps and watching the flank. We swap when someone is tired. Not when someone is spent.
say sable | Voss has three relay stations feeding the dais. South relay, north lift relay, and the bridge itself.
say ivo | And the lifts. The evacuation lifts run on a separate feed. Whatever we cut, we don't cut those.
say pip | There are people in those lifts. Ministry clerks, conscripts, families from the lower wards. Voss called it 'relocation'.
say narr | (All eight travel together. Choose your active four with Formation in the menu at any time outside battle.)
formation
objective sable | Release the south relay (west) and reroute the north lift relay (east) without cutting lift power.
@end

@scene D09_LIFT_CREW
if flag:d09_relay_s,flag:d09_relay_n both
say worker | Lift's still running. Whatever you're doing down there, keep doing it that way.
end
label both
say worker | Both relays quiet and the lift never dropped. I've been doing this nineteen years. First time anyone asked me before touching the feed.
@end

@scene D09_RELAY_S
if flag:d09_relay_s done
say narr | A synchronization relay, singing the coronation note. Its housing matches the trial relay at Nacre.
say ivo | Same trick as the trial. Spread the load, don't slam it off.
say oriel | And stop if it answers no.
choice | Release it slowly (the Nacre method) -> slow | Smash the housing -> smash | Leave it -> leave
label smash
sfx FX004
shake 0.4
say narr | Tessa's hand is on the housing before anyone else moves - then she stops.
say tessa | No. If it's somebody in there, I'm not doing to them what Rook wants to do to everyone.
say narr | (The relay is still singing. Try the slow release.)
end
label slow
sfx FX024
wait 0.4
say narr | The note bends, then settles, then goes out like a lamp being turned down rather than blown. Somewhere far above, one bell misses its beat.
set d09_relay_s
say ivo | South relay is resting. It will wake if somebody asks it to.
objective sable | South relay released. Reroute the north lift relay (east from the aqueduct), then head north to the Soldiers' Walk.
end
label done
say narr | The south relay is dim and quiet.
label leave
@end

@scene D09_LIFT_RIDERS
say survivor | The lift stopped between floors, then came down here. They said the ministry needs the power. We're not going anywhere until someone turns the lift back on.
@end

@scene D09_LIFT_SAFE
say survivor | It moved! It's taking the next group up to the river gate. Thank you - whoever you are.
@end

@scene D09_RELAY_N
if flag:d09_relay_n done
say narr | The north relay feeds both the dais line and the occupied lift. A lever can switch the lift to the old aqueduct feed.
say ivo | Lift first. Then the relay. The other order drops a car full of people.
choice | Switch the lift to the aqueduct feed, then quiet the relay -> right | Quiet the relay first -> wrong | Leave it -> leave
label wrong
sfx FX004
say narr | The lift lights flicker as the load wavers. You stop at once. The lift holds - barely. (Lift first.)
end
label right
sfx FX010
wait 0.3
say narr | The lift cable shudders, catches the old feed, and starts to climb. Only then does the relay go dark.
set d09_relay_n
say pip | That's the ministry's own lift, carrying the ministry's own clerks out. Nobody's going to write that down.
say sable | I will.
objective sable | North relay rerouted. Go north to the Soldiers' Walk.
end
label done
say narr | The north relay is dark. The lift runs on the aqueduct feed.
label leave
@end

@scene D09_SOLDIERS
say soldier | Don't - we're not fighting. The ceiling came down on the barracks when the bells started. Three of us are pinned.
choice | Help them out -> help | Not now -> later
label help
fade out 0.4
say narr | It takes all eight of you and a borrowed crowbar. Nobody is badly hurt.
fade in 0.4
set d09_rescue
say soldier | Voss told us the dais would 'end the instability'. He didn't say what he meant by it.
say soldier | Take this. Field kit. We're going up with the lift.
give I003 2
give I023 1
end
label later
say soldier | ...We'll be here.
@end

@scene D09_SOLDIERS_AFTER
say soldier | We'll get the others moving to the lift. If you see the Marshal - he isn't going to stop.
@end

@scene D09_WARNING once
say narr | Beyond the Soldiers' Walk the corridor opens onto the Marshal Bridge. Past it, the Crown Dais.
say oriel | Listen. Whatever happens past this door, some of it will not be undone.
say dain | Then we write down where we were before it.
backup pre_dais
say narr | (A protected backup has been written: "Before the Crown Dais". It is separate from your save slots and can be loaded from Load at any time.)
say narr | (This is the last point where you can freely leave the Conduit. Rest and save at the lamp if you need to.)
objective sable | Cross the Marshal Bridge (north) and stop Voss before he takes the network.
@end

@scene D09_VOSS once
music silence
show voss 19 14 down voss
say voss | Stop there. You are standing on the only bridge that holds this country together.
say sable | You're holding it together with people's names, Marshal.
say voss | I am replacing a hundred unstable relays with one stable authority. No more outages. No more hosts deciding they would rather not.
say oriel | That last part is the point for you. Not the outages.
say voss | Order is a kindness to people who cannot afford chaos.
say pip | You signed my forgeries' death certificates yourself, sir. Twice. I checked.
say voss | Then you know I read everything I sign. Guards - protect the Marshal.
say narr | Voss raises the command baton and points at a protector.
battle B09 noflee
set b09_done
music M020
say narr | Voss staggers back against the bridge relay. The baton cracks.
say voss | You think you have won something. Rook is already at the dais. He does not need my authority. He wants none at all.
say narr | Voss retreats into the central apparatus below the bridge. The hatch seals behind him.
hide voss
say dain | Let him go. Rook first.
say ivo | The bridge relay is exposed now. Quiet it and the dais door opens.
chapter CH11
xp 520
level_floor 23
objective dain | Quiet the bridge relay, then climb to the Crown Dais.
@end

@scene D09_RELAY_B
if flag:d09_relay_b done
say narr | The bridge relay. The third synchronization line.
sfx FX024
say narr | Ivo and Oriel release it the way they did in Nacre. It goes dim. The dais door groans open.
set d09_relay_b
say ivo | Three visible relays. All dark.
say oriel | Visible.
objective dain | Climb to the Crown Dais.
end
label done
say narr | The bridge relay is dark.
@end
